# the sticks for m48_joy.keys ("T N,X,Y,B": stick N with one-shots of X
# and Y microseconds and the buttons B, 1 the first and 2 the second;
# "T N,off" takes it away).  570 is a stick's middle here.
# the first stick, there when F5 looks for it at 32 and 34; its left
# before that is not seen
31.00 0,100,570,0
31.60 0,570,570,0
# left, right, up, down, right and down at once
35.00 0,100,570,0
35.60 0,570,570,0
36.00 0,1100,570,0
36.60 0,570,570,0
37.00 0,570,100,0
37.60 0,570,570,0
38.00 0,570,1100,0
38.60 0,570,570,0
39.00 0,1100,1100,0
39.60 0,570,570,0
# its first button, its second, the first twice in a row
40.00 0,570,570,1
40.30 0,570,570,0
41.00 0,570,570,2
41.30 0,570,570,0
42.00 0,570,570,1
42.10 0,570,570,0
42.20 0,570,570,1
42.30 0,570,570,0
# just inside the left edge (half the middle), then just outside
43.00 0,300,570,0
43.50 0,270,570,0
43.80 0,570,570,0
# the second stick, there when F6 looks for it at 44.5 and 45.5
44.00 1,600,500,0
46.00 1,100,500,0
46.60 1,600,500,0
47.00 1,600,1000,1
47.60 1,600,500,0
# both at once
48.00 0,1100,570,0
48.00 1,600,100,0
48.60 0,570,570,0
48.60 1,600,500,0
# the first side's stick not wanted from 52: it gives nothing
53.00 0,100,570,0
53.60 0,570,570,0
# the first stick gone when F5 looks at 57 (wanted again, not there: the
# keys); the second held left while F6 measures it at 59, back to its
# middle, left again, and gone while wanted
56.00 0,off
58.00 1,100,500,0
60.00 1,600,500,0
61.00 1,100,500,0
61.50 1,600,500,0
# (not at 62.00: that falls into a read of the original's timer routine,
# 0.46 ms after its call at 61.99954 while it still polls the port, so the
# original loses the stick in the middle of a read; the port's script
# changes the sticks between two calls)
62.10 1,off
